{
 "version": 3,
 "lexicon_version": "v2",
 "phase": "10.1",
 "query_rules": true,
 "purpose": "Map technician/driver/SAE J1939 vocabulary to the manual's formal ECU terminology, to close the free-text symptom-retrieval gap (mid-sem feedback). Extends the Phase 8.2 lexicon; v1 entries are kept verbatim.",
 "provenance_values": [
  "manual_term",
  "sae_j1939",
  "general_technician"
 ],
 "rules": [
  "Aliases are SUBSYSTEM-level (system_aliases) or DESCRIPTION-level (term_synonyms). A subsystem-level alias must be correct for EVERY record in that subsystem; otherwise it is description-level (Phase 8.2 rule).",
  "Aliases are NEVER derived from step text: step boilerplate is shared across hundreds of DTCs and aliasing it would re-collapse near-duplicate families.",
  "Index side: BM25 ONLY (--aliases bm25). Phase 8.2 config C6 showed that aliasing the dense text merges near-duplicate families.",
  "provenance dev_driven is 0 by construction: no entry is derived from a DEV miss. The frozen TEST split and the forthcoming independent technician query set were not read when authoring v2.",
  "Query-side rewrite rules (cylinder ordinals, valve/switch state negation) live in src/lexicon.py and are enabled by query_rules=true; they run BEFORE BM25 expansion and never touch the dense query or the gate."
 ],
 "not_covered": [
  "Warning-lamp language (warning light, dash light, check engine, MIL): the tokens 'lamp', 'mil' and 'warning' do not occur in the BM25 corpus at all, because bm25_text() carries description/cause/effect/checkpoints/circuit text but not the MIL field. An alias here would expand to a term with no postings, so none was added.",
  "Abnormal-noise language (knocking, rattle, whistle, whine): 'noise', 'knock', 'rattle' and 'whistle' do not occur in the corpus.",
  "White/blue smoke: no smoke vocabulary exists in the corpus. Only black smoke is mapped, to soot/particulate filter, and that mapping is a diagnostic inference rather than a synonym."
 ],
